# Fixed defect 2431, 2026-11-10, lane b30-pkg, the shapes beside it: one
# package under two aliases, `core` in the program's catalogue and `text` in
# `json`'s own (panel 235's R3), the brackets forgotten in `json`'s files.
#
# A bare `use` of a package's file is told the entry its own catalogue
# names, as its own `use` lines write it: `use text/strconv` is told
# `use <text>/strconv`, and `use text as t` the modules at `text`'s root.
# `use core/strconv` is told only that `json` has no module `core/strconv`:
# `core` is the program's alias, which no line of `json` can write, so it is
# never offered there. The modules are `vendor/json/a.hero`, `b.hero` and
# `c.hero`, each marked where it is told.
use <json>/a
use <json>/b
use <json>/c

function main()
    print(a.word() + b.word() + c.word())
